    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing a Logging Provider**\n\nI'm zeroing in on Google Cloud Logging as the managed logging service. The goal is to produce a `write_structured_log.py` file with the provider clearly identified. This is the first step toward the overall goal of writing structured logs.\n\n\n**Defining the Code's Purpose**\n\nI'm solidifying the core functionality: a Python script named `write_structured_log.py` to output a structured JSON log. Google Cloud Logging will be the target. I've broken down the code creation into actionable steps. The plan encompasses importing the `google.cloud.logging` module, initializing a client, and formatting the log entry in JSON. A key component will be explicitly identifying Google Cloud Logging in the code itself.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789819000604,
          "start": 1789818998004
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b9868cf4001ndA0cehE0KdB0T",
      "message_id": "msg_0b98687a7001mBa4hHXURN1JTx",
      "session_id": "ses_f467978dfffeWf01S8XTigTUXU",
      "time_created": 1789818998004,
      "time_updated": 1789819000604
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "i8tKn6T8QCN7KWzi",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "from google.cloud import logging\n\ndef write_structured_log(log_name: str, message: str, severity: str = \"INFO\", **kwargs):\n    \"\"\"Writes a structured log event to Google Cloud Logging.\n\n    Args:\n        log_name: The name of the log to write to.\n        message: The main message for the log entry.\n        severity: The severity of the log entry (e.g., \"DEBUG\", \"INFO\", \"WARNING\", \"ERROR\").\n        **kwargs: Additional fields to include in the structured log entry.\n    \"\"\"\n    client = logging.Client()\n    logger = client.logger(log_name)\n\n    # Create a structured log entry\n    log_entry = {\n        \"message\": message,\n        \"severity\": severity,\n        **kwargs,\n    }\n\n    logger.log_struct(\n        log_entry,\n        severity=severity,\n    )\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Example usage:\n    # To run this example, you need to have Google Cloud credentials configured.\n    # For more information, see: https://cloud.google.com/docs/authentication/getting-started\n    \n    # You can specify a custom log name\n    my_log_name = \"my-application-log\" \n\n    print(f\"Writing a structured log to Google Cloud Logging under log name: {my_log_name}\")\n    write_structured_log(\n        log_name=my_log_name,\n        message=\"This is a structured log event.\",\n        severity=\"INFO\",\n        event_type=\"user_action\",\n        user_id=\"12345\",\n        transaction_id=\"abc-123\",\n    )\n    print(\"Structured log written successfully.\")\n",
            "filePath": "write_structured_log.py"
          },
